{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-material4-v3-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-01","runId":"chemie-material4-v3-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-material4-v3-targeted-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-material4-v3-targeted-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:2b4d85280ea1c758aa980e8517f462b3c7b5533e79e38c5ad50c1592b5756762","bookDigest":"sha256:e501cc7cb865f079fd49eae07cd7e85923c9c0b6172fb38e410ef54a5020a6c1","goalId":"f85b4651-50ea-5b42-b193-3465c05257a7","goalFingerprint":"sha256:9ffb4363e6e864a302afd1ae4ae743606b402cdde234375ccc281b9043c34ac8","pageFingerprint":"sha256:d4da343674a34f2a6116e44273f5e6cd735f2fc4ba4d7b251732097bcb93aaa5","currentTitleDe":"Molekülorbital-Modelle anwenden","currentTitleEn":"Apply molecular orbital models","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann einfache MO-Diagramme (z. B. O2, N2) interpretieren und Bindungsordnung ableiten.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can interpret simple MO diagrams (e.g. O2, N2) and derive bond order.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"In einem vorgegebenen Valenz-MO-Schema ergibt die halbe Differenz bindender und antibindender Elektronenzahlen die Bindungsordnung; ungepaarte Elektronen erlauben eine begrenzte Aussage zum Magnetismus.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"In a supplied valence MO scheme, half the difference between bonding and antibonding electron counts gives bond order; unpaired electrons support a bounded magnetic interpretation.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person liest die tatsächlichen Besetzungen eines N2- oder O2-Schemas, zählt selbst und begründet Bindungsordnung und gegebenenfalls ungepaarte Elektronen.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner reads the actual N2 or O2 orbital occupancies, independently counts electrons and justifies bond order and, where applicable, unpaired electrons.","transferExpectationDe":"Beim Übergang zu N2+ oder O2+ bestimmt die lernende Person aus dem jeweils höchsten besetzten Orbital die geänderte Besetzung und erklärt den unterschiedlichen Einfluss auf die Bindungsordnung.","transferExpectationEn":"For N2+ or O2+, the learner determines the changed occupancy from the highest occupied orbital and explains its different effect on bond order."},"rationale":"Actual bounded V3 current-context review retains this clear, scientifically accurate bilingual description without changing its scope. The two whole N2/O2 cases now explicitly assess diagram reading, electron counting, justified bond order and fresh molecular-ion transfer, with no chemical experiment required. The old false retained-practice obligation is removed in both languages. All other material fields equal the frozen v1 whole objects. N2 bonding8/antibonding2 gives BO3; N2+ removes bonding sigma2p and gives2.5. O2 bonding8/antibonding4 gives2; O2+ removes pi-star and gives2.5. Supplied qualitative orbital orders and unpaired-electron interpretation remain bounded, not exact energy/rate predictions. Current V3 operative bindings resolve to the same exact already wholly reviewed V2 material bytes and unchanged whole profile. Targeted current-binding review retains this finding; no new independent vote on the old fourteen is claimed.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-material4-v3-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-02","runId":"chemie-material4-v3-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-material4-v3-targeted-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-material4-v3-targeted-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:2b4d85280ea1c758aa980e8517f462b3c7b5533e79e38c5ad50c1592b5756762","bookDigest":"sha256:e501cc7cb865f079fd49eae07cd7e85923c9c0b6172fb38e410ef54a5020a6c1","goalId":"b8d3b453-d638-5518-aab0-d84ec2e8567c","goalFingerprint":"sha256:7cfe6610ec81b9510eebe1a403f40740cdb6cf50176512a16397f87b103a6358","pageFingerprint":"sha256:31ee65cebd597481035268a3b64c6c6e999db27fd6c0229db99b8cbff954d1e4","currentTitleDe":"Reaktivität aromatischer Systeme begründen","currentTitleEn":"Explain aromatic reactivity","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann die Reaktivität aromatischer Systeme anhand ihrer Elektronendelokalisierung begründen.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can explain the reactivity of aromatic systems in terms of their electron delocalization.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Delokalisierung stabilisiert das aromatische System; eine elektrophile Substitution verliert die Aromatizität vorübergehend und stellt sie durch Protonenabgabe wieder her.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"Delocalization stabilizes the aromatic system; electrophilic substitution temporarily loses aromaticity and restores it through proton loss.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person verfolgt Elektronenverteilung, Ladung und Bindungen eines vorgegebenen sigma-Komplexes und begründet die Rückbildung des aromatischen Systems statt einer pauschalen Reaktionsträgheit.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner tracks electron distribution, charge and bonds in a supplied sigma complex and explains restoration of aromaticity rather than claiming blanket inertness.","transferExpectationDe":"An einem neuen NO2+-Papierfall vergleicht die lernende Person Protonenabgabe und eine ausdrücklich hypothetische Abfangreaktion und erklärt anhand einer gegebenen Hydrierung, weshalb aromatisch nicht niemals Addition bedeutet.","transferExpectationEn":"In a fresh NO2+ paper case, the learner compares proton loss with an explicitly hypothetical capture step and uses supplied hydrogenation to explain why aromatic does not mean addition is impossible."},"rationale":"Actual bounded V3 current-context review retains this clear, scientifically accurate bilingual description without changing its scope. The whole NO2+ paper case now states explicitly that neither experimental nitration nor hydrogenation is required. Atom/charge balance and restored cyclic delocalization remain the assessed performance. C6H6 + NO2+ to C6H5NO2 + H+ conserves atoms and charge; hypothetical chloride capture is labelled a model alternative rather than a competing laboratory nitration claim. Supplied hydrogenation limits any universal prohibition of addition. Only the two assessmentBoundary fields changed; no new practical duty or task quota is introduced. Current V3 operative bindings resolve to the same exact already wholly reviewed V2 material bytes and unchanged whole profile. Targeted current-binding review retains this finding; no new independent vote on the old fourteen is claimed.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-material4-v3-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-03","runId":"chemie-material4-v3-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-material4-v3-targeted-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-material4-v3-targeted-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:2b4d85280ea1c758aa980e8517f462b3c7b5533e79e38c5ad50c1592b5756762","bookDigest":"sha256:e501cc7cb865f079fd49eae07cd7e85923c9c0b6172fb38e410ef54a5020a6c1","goalId":"28c90c6a-3020-5c51-ac40-d802f3f12d2d","goalFingerprint":"sha256:5e7666abb7cd2c4c761356fcd30cccad0080ed13ebcaeb84fb8683e8b420f9c5","pageFingerprint":"sha256:0615cd90f0de8d2fb0cc84970706807ab73000ac8fd1082a0db6344ef4030ee8","currentTitleDe":"Titrationskurven datengestützt deuten","currentTitleEn":"Interpret titration curves using data","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann aus bereitgestellten Titrationsdaten den Verlauf einer Titrationskurve, den Äquivalenzbereich und vorhandene Halbäquivalenz- oder Pufferbereiche erkennen, mit den jeweils pH-bestimmenden Teilchen erklären und daraus begrenzte Aussagen zu Stoffklasse und geeigneten Indikatoren ableiten.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can use supplied titration data to identify curve behaviour, the equivalence region and any half-equivalence or buffer regions, explain them using the pH-controlling species, and derive bounded conclusions about substance class and suitable indicators.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Titrationskurven verknüpfen Stoffmengenverhältnis und Säure-Base-Gleichgewichte mit Anfangs-, Puffer-, Äquivalenz- und Überschussbereichen; Neutralität und Äquivalenz sind verschiedene Begriffe.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"Titration curves connect mole ratios and acid-base equilibria with initial, buffer, equivalence and excess regions; neutrality and equivalence are distinct concepts.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person deutet vorgegebene starke und schwache Säure- oder Basenkurven, lokalisiert charakteristische Bereiche und begründet einen passenden Indikator aus dem tatsächlichen steilen Bereich.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner interprets supplied strong and weak acid or base curves, locates characteristic regions and justifies an indicator using the actual steep interval.","transferExpectationDe":"Bei einer umgekehrten Titrationsrichtung, verändertem pKw oder einer mehrstufigen Glycinkurve begründet die lernende Person die veränderte qualitative Deutung, ohne Äquivalenz stets mit pH 7 oder einem beliebigen Zwischenpunkt mit guter Pufferung gleichzusetzen.","transferExpectationEn":"For reversed titration direction, changed pKw or a multistage glycine curve, the learner explains the changed qualitative interpretation without equating equivalence with pH 7 or any intermediate point with effective buffering."},"rationale":"Actual bounded V3 current-context review retains this clear, scientifically accurate bilingual description without changing its scope. Actual V3 changes exactly two rubric-to-expectation array elements, with all other whole material fields and all four whole profiles equal to the actual V2 input. In T05-C1 the supplied temperature-neutrality explanation now contributes to q3, matching that expectation. In POLY-QUALITATIVE-C1 the class/curve identity and jump-count limitation now contributes to q1, matching the bounded curve-inference expectation; it no longer falsely claims indicator q3. All twenty current rubric links were independently compared with actual questions, full-credit performances and the unchanged q1/q2/q3/q4 profile. The acid/base pool still provides indicator/endpoint/neutrality evidence for q3 and strength/amount/class comparisons for q4; no additional case, calculation or quota is introduced. All five operative assignments now point to the corrected V3 collection, not old individual V2 copies. Existing quantitative originals remain separate, interpretation tables/numbers are unchanged, and no practical execution is required for this data-reading goal.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-material4-v3-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-04","runId":"chemie-material4-v3-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-material4-v3-targeted-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-material4-v3-targeted-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:2b4d85280ea1c758aa980e8517f462b3c7b5533e79e38c5ad50c1592b5756762","bookDigest":"sha256:e501cc7cb865f079fd49eae07cd7e85923c9c0b6172fb38e410ef54a5020a6c1","goalId":"188bd684-e894-5753-8a50-798220b04d97","goalFingerprint":"sha256:e87f813cff7a6d79e6985fd630f3d60f484542c1e8184d82b14b410bab1db3fe","pageFingerprint":"sha256:8676d1f1a51ac1e3604e8622cf2631fb6128743d098f7a5d68521771234819a8","currentTitleDe":"Farbstoffe als Motor der chemischen Industrie beurteilen","currentTitleEn":"Assess dyes as a driver of the chemical industry","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann die wirtschaftliche Bedeutung der Farbstoffe für die Entwicklung der chemischen Industrie beurteilen.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can assess the economic significance of dyes for the development of the chemical industry.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Industrielle Farbstoffentwicklung verbindet chemische Innovation mit Investition, Anwendungen, Wettbewerb und sozialen Folgen; unterschiedliche Quellen belegen unterschiedliche Ausschnitte.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"Industrial dye development connects chemical innovation with investment, applications, competition and social effects; different sources establish different parts of this history.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person beurteilt die wirtschaftliche Bedeutung des synthetischen Indigos anhand tatsächlich zugänglicher historischer Quellen, ordnet Herkunft und Interessen ein und trennt belegte Investition von unbelegtem Gewinn.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner assesses the economic significance of synthetic indigo using actual accessible historical sources, considers provenance and interests and distinguishes documented investment from unproven profit.","transferExpectationDe":"Für den neuen Indanthren-Fall begründet die lernende Person, wie Eigenschaften neue Anwendungen und innerbetrieblichen Wettbewerb ermöglichen, und benennt zusätzliche Belege für eine belastbare langfristige Markt- oder Gewinnbehauptung.","transferExpectationEn":"For the new Indanthrene case, the learner explains how properties enable applications and internal competition and identifies extra evidence needed for a defensible long-term market or profit claim."},"rationale":"Actual bounded V3 current-context review retains this clear, scientifically accurate bilingual description without changing its scope. The whole actual-source historical case now correctly assesses source-critical economic judgment and transfer without a chemical experiment. Source interests, attributed investment versus revenue/profit and missing independent financial records remain explicit. The earlier actual BASF and museum source review by this reviewer remains a bounded unchanged source reference, not a new financial audit or claim that a learner researched. All other material fields equal the frozen v1 whole case. Current V3 operative bindings resolve to the same exact already wholly reviewed V2 material bytes and unchanged whole profile. Targeted current-binding review retains this finding; no new independent vote on the old fourteen is claimed.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
